{
  "_about": [
    "SINGLE source of truth for air-defense data in DCS:OPT (backend + frontend).",
    "Backend: reference/loader.py. Frontend: src/data/airDefense.ts imports this file directly.",
    "Replaces sam_threat_ranges.json, unit_extractor.SAM_THREAT_RANGES, and the SAM tables that were in",
    "AegisSetupPanel / ThreatLibraryTab / ThreatCard (they disagreed with each other).",
    "",
    "Fields per system:",
    "  role       'sam' = weapon ring (goes in threats[]); 'ew' = early-warning radar (goes in ewRadars[])",
    "  rangeKm    ring radius. SAM = max engagement; EW = NOMINAL max detection (approx=true) - terrain and",
    "             radar horizon cut this hard for low flyers, so it is an upper bound, not a promise",
    "  types      EXACT DCS unit type names that put a ring on the map (keep to one-ish unit per site",
    "             where possible, every matching unit draws its own ring)",
    "  match      case-insensitive SUBSTRING keys for loose lookup (threat library / kneeboard card).",
    "             ORDER MATTERS: the systems list is scanned top-down, first hit wins, so specific",
    "             entries (SA-17, Strela-10, S-300 variants) sit above generic ones (SA-11, Strela-1, S-300)",
    "  aegis      present when AEGIS IADS knows the system. Values MIRROR AEGIS.SYSTEM_DB in",
    "             assets/scripts/aegis-iads-v0.8.4-beta.lua (identical in v0.9.1) - the engine is",
    "             authoritative, edit there first. wez/nez/actRange in NM, altMin/altMax in feet MSL.",
    "             trackRadars = unit types that identify the site for the AEGIS auto-setup panel."
  ],
